    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d226">

                <pb facs="0314" n="234" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg234"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1901-11-25"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November 25, 1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 714.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Choate’s dispatch No. 640,
                    of August 14 last, and to previous correspondence, with reference to the claim
                    of Charles Lillywhite, I have the honor to inclose herewith the copy of a note
                    which I have received from the Marquis of Lansdowne, relative to the above case,
                    stating that, in view of the special hardships imposed upon Lillywhite, His
                    Majesty’s Government are prepared to grant him the sum of £600, by way of
                    solatium, and also the cost of his return journey to New Zealand.</p>
                <p>I have caused the information in question to be communicated to Mr. Barrett,
                    counsel for Mr. Lillywhite, who is not, I believe, in England at present.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry White.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d226-a1.xml" xpointer="d226-a1"/>
            </div>
